  "text": "Recipe: Veggie Loaded Uthappam\nCreator: Dr Sirisha Potluri\nCategory: Uthappam\nIngredients: sorghum, brown rice, toor dal, methi seeds, red rice poha, ginger, green chillies, cumin seeds, carrot, onion\nCooking methods: soak, grind, ferment, cook\nInstructions: SORGUM DOSA BATTER\nSoak these overnight: 4 parts sorghum, 1 part brown rice, 1 part toor dal, 1 Tbsp methi seeds.\nNext day, grind them with 2 Tbsp soaked atukulu (red rice poha), ginger, green chillies and cumin seeds. Ferment for 6-8 hours.\nThen add finely grated or minced veggies of our choice, e.g., carrot, onion, ginger, ...\nUTHAPAM\nSpread batter on a hot non-stick pan or cast iron tawa. Cook both sides to make a Veggie Loaded Uthapam.",
